#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""MiniCut Patch 47 - Round controls for effect parameters (dials, speed wheel, 3D box)

* Angles (Angle, Direction, Rotate, Roll ...) are small dials like the rotation dial of the Basic tab. Angles that follow each other share one row. Double click resets; Shift = 15 degree steps.
* Spin (deg / s) is a speed wheel: drag the OUTER ring to set the speed (top = still, clockwise = faster, the other way = reverse, Shift = steps of 15, mouse wheel = steps of 5); the INNER disc shows how far it has turned by now (clip time x speed) as a needle and in degrees.
* Cube, Card, Sphere and Cylinder: Tilt X and Turn Y are one small 3D box. Drag it and it turns like the result (same rotation and faces as the Cube effect, including the spin). A white dot marks the top-left corner of the picture on each face. Roll is a dial and Spin a wheel in the same row.
* 29 effects use round controls, the others keep their sliders. If a round control cannot be built, the card falls back to the sliders.

Files changed: minicut/workspace/effects_panel.py, minicut/workspace/fx_controls.py
  python Patch/apply_47_round_controls.py --check      (look only, change nothing)
  python Patch/apply_47_round_controls.py              (install)
  python Patch/apply_47_round_controls.py --revert     (put the files back from the backup)
Close MiniCut before installing. The MiniCut Launcher can do all of this for you.
"""
import base64, datetime, hashlib, json, os, py_compile, shutil, sys, zlib
